n 2018  and it's the first real-life example of  this coaster type  that was already featured in this game  from 2004 so  honestly that's kind of crazy and i  think there are a lot of cases  like that there's also the uh ball  coaster or the coaster ball  in the game which is basically the real  world intamin zack spin  only the first intimins x pin ever was  built in 2005  and this game is again from 2004 so  it definitely seems like that like the  developers of this game  not only went out of their way to add a  lot of existing roller coaster and ride  types in the world but they also looked  for what kind of prototypes were  in development and weren't out yet so i  think that's super cool and i think  for that reason there are still some  coaster types that  you would have to play roller coaster  queen 3 for because you don't find them  in any other game yet  and i mean i say yes because i kind of  hope that these sorts of roller coasters  will still be added  maybe in future games in the coaster  simulation genre but i think so far  roller coaster can three is pretty  unique in that it's the only  3d game that features so many rides and  roller coasters  so i think that's still really worth  playing for that reason as well  and finally of course i think there's  just fun  in the challenge of trying to work with  what the game gives you  instead of taking all of these modded  scenery pieces that basically  sometimes already build things for you  um  at least i've been enjoying trying to  get back into these old scenery sets and  seeing what you can make out of it  and there's always a cool sense of  accomplishment from  building something intricate and  detailed from these  pretty basic pieces at least when  compared to all of the custom scenery  stuff  anyway to go back to the coaster that  i'm building here  well it's not really the coaster anymore  the castle was finished at this point  and one last thing that i wanted to add  in  was a small town at the foot of these  hills just to kind of give an idea of  the  sheer scale of the castle this was a  little bit inspired by the romanian town  of brasov which is  very close to the real-life dracula  castle and  it's just a it's just a nice romanian  town with lots of  red roof buildings um and some baroque  architecture stuff like that so very  generally inspired by that i decided to  build this town but of course it's not  quite as detailed or exactly in the same  style  although again i have to say i was  pleasantly surprised with how flexible  some of the roof pieces turned out to be  there's a set of wild west  roofs which are recolorable and just  have these nice wooden shingles that can  be used for tile roofs which i'm using  here  and in this case i made them orange  because this orange  red-ish tint is just a thing you see a  lot in romania  but it's something that i think can work  for many different themes and it's one  of those  versatile scenery sets that even though  the game doesn't feature  that much scenery and a lot of it might  not be recolorable  i think you can still do a lot with some  of the basic sets so  actually i think the western sets in  this game are my favorites because  whenever you're building anything that's  wooden or you need some recolorable  roofs or stuff for  the western set basically has all of the  main pieces that you're looking for  i think also back in the day especially  in the early days  of community creations of roller coaster  country western themes were always the  ones that were  most well executed and most realistic  looking  and i think it's a clear well example of  just the in-game scenery sets working  really well for  what you need to do with them to be fair  western is also kind of a basic theme  but i think it works alright uh another  fun thing that i think people tend to  forget a lot when they're playing this  game is that  many of the scenery pieces aren't even  in the building section  you have a lot of useful fences for  instance that you can place in  in whatever locations you want and  there's also this terrain elements  uh menu where you can add big blocks of  terrain but you can also find some gates  some various steel and wooden gates and  stuff like that  that you can place over coasters or uses  custom supports  or whatever you want and these i think  are  some of the uh the things that you don't  find as much in roller coaster country  builds but that you can do a lot with  i think back in the days that i was  getting into roller coaster country  seriously and getting into the real  community of it  so sometime around 2009 or 2010  there were always players who were  trying to make the most out of the  in-game pieces and really playing  in the vanilla or the ncs style as some  people called it or no cs  um and i think a particular example is  eloria  aka stephen who's made a lot of indoor  swimming pools and theme parks and  things like that  and i remember watching a lot of their  videos that was  honestly my childhood i think there's  also moonkin for the win  of course who made the box series which  i recently did a coaster inspired by in  planet coaster  but the basic box was also done without  any custom scenery and i think  a lot of these videos show that even  though there was a super alive modding  community for roller coaster country  there's always been this push by many  people  to also keep it vanilla and see what you  can do with the base game  i also got a comment from somebody on my  last video about piece of prestige who  is an  old roller coaster country player who  always focused on doing stuff without  custom scenery  and they were wondering if i knew his  youtube channel which is kind of funny  because i actually  still talk to him on a somewhat regular  basis um but yeah  highly recommend his videos too if  you're if you're in 2020 and you want to  live that 2010 life and go back into  roller coaster [ __ ] 3 builds  i recommend all of this stuff just  alloria moonkin for the win piece of  prestige these are just some examples  but i think there's a lot out there um  and i think even for planet coaster  players  you can find a lot of inspiration in  rollercoaster tycoon 3 builds  that community was very small but it was  super passionate about theme parks and  i think even more than the planet  coaster community it was very  focused on constructive criticism and  trying to raise everybody up  in a sense that people are always  helping each other get better at the  game  and discover tricks and tips and things  like this and i think  inevitably the planet coaster community  has lost some of that drive  in a sense that it's just a bigger group  of people and it's a bit more casual  and a bit more focused on fun because  not gonna lie the roller coaster country  community was a bit dramatic at times  and  um super passionate about this topic  but still it was really cool to to see  how  people just just got this communal  spirit from this game  and focused so much on trying to make  everybody better at it and i think  as a result of that there are some  rollercoaster 3 builds which  nowadays can even be great inspiration  for planet coaster  they might not look that great  graphically  but there are some really some really  great thought behind it in all of the  details  and composition and layouts for theme  parks and such  i can't really name anything off the top  of my head that i think  is is a great straight example for  planet coaster builds but i know that  personally i've always had a folder of  builds by leonidas who you can find  still on new elements and also has an  old photobucket account  whereas lots of really great roller  coaster queen 3 builds  and they're also just great youtube  videos there's  arm puzzle which is one of my favorite  coasters ever built in the game  um you can find on mike sheets channel  who's still active in planet coast and  planet zoo some really great  coasters in rct3 as well and of course  i don't want to plug myself too much but  there's my old youtube channel called  silverad archive where i have a lot of  my old rollercoaster  3 stuff saved as well as of course some  videos on this channel  so i think there's a lot of stuff to go  back for and even if you already own  planet coaster  or if you don't own planet coaster and  you're still sticking with roller  coaster country  there's been so much amazing content in  this game that honestly  i can just talk about for hours and just  let my stream of consciousness go on  about  unfortunately that's something i can't  really do in this video so  i'm just gonna leave it here and share  with you guys a quick cinematic clip and  pov  of this coaster hope you guys enjoyed  this little  off the cuff roller coaster 3 video  again  um i'm sorry if it's not quite as  in-depth or  thought out as my videos usually are but  i figured after preparing all of this  for the launch live stream i didn't want  to just  leave it in the void and do nothing with  it um so here you guys go  hope you enjoyed and i'll see you on the  next one  [Music]  you  [Music]  so  [Music]  hey  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

